<title>USA: Goodyear to hire 125 engineers.</title>
<headline>Goodyear to hire 125 engineers.</headline>
<dateline>AKRON, Ohio 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Goodyear Tire &amp; Rubber Co said Thursday that it will hire 125 new engineers and scientists to augment its staffs in North America and Europe.</p>
<p>The company said the hiring reflects its growth into new international markets and &quot;unprecedented&quot; levels of new product and process development.</p>
<p>The company said that about 80 of the new hires will work at its Akron, Ohio, Technical Center, with the rest at Goodyear's European Technical Center in Colmar-Berg, Luxembourg.  Goodyear said it will spend approximately $26 million in the next year to support these staffing additions and will recruit globally for them.</p>
<p>The company's total research and development expenditures in 1996 were $375 million, it said.</p>
